# Skeleton

A pulsing placeholder that holds the shape of content while it loads.
Basecoat ships no component — it is `animate-pulse` plus the `accent`
token and sizing utilities, written inline. Compose several to mirror a
layout.

<%= embed :skeleton, :default %>

```html
<div class="bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-4 w-48" aria-hidden="true"></div>
<div class="bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-4 w-32" aria-hidden="true"></div>
```

## When to use

- A page region is loading and its layout is known — rows, cards,
  headings get a placeholder of the same shape, so nothing jumps
  when content lands.

## When not to use

- Content that might come back empty — resolve straight to the empty
  state; a skeleton promises content (see the *Feedback* pattern
  page).
- Unknown layout — use `spinner`.
- In-flight button actions — the button's `loading` param.

## Anatomy and options

A single block: `animate-pulse` for the pulse, `bg-accent` for the
fill, and sizing/shape utilities for the dimensions — `h-4 w-32`,
`rounded-full size-10` (avatar), `h-24 w-full` (card). Compose several
to mirror a layout: one per heading, row or cell, in the same container
the real content will use.

## Do and don't

- Do match the real content's dimensions — same heights, same grid,
  same gaps. The page must not reflow on arrival.
- Do keep skeleton groups brief: placeholder the first screenful,
  not an entire long list.
- Don't approximate text with one big block — one bar per line reads
  as text; a slab reads as an image.
- Don't combine with a spinner or progress bar for the same region.

## Accessibility and content

- Mark each placeholder `aria-hidden="true"` — screen readers skip it;
  announce loading via the region's live text or a `role="status"`
  spinner when one exists elsewhere.
- Uses the `accent` token, so it stays visible in both themes without
  any per-theme tuning.
